    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Glomus tumour",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Axial T1-weighted (Fig. &lt;&lt;56732&gt;&gt;) and fat-saturated T2-weighted (Fig. &lt;&lt;56731&gt;&gt;) imaging of the upper arm. There is a large T2-hyperintense, T1-isointense lesion within the superficial soft tissues, closely related to the skin. On ultrasound imaging (Fig. &lt;&lt;56730&gt;&gt;), there is marked vascularity that is typical of these lesions. Although a subungual location is most common, glomus tumours can occur anywhere, as in this case.",
    "source": "Dr Huw Walters and Dr Rajat Chowdhury, Department of Radiology, Nuffield Orthopaedic Centre, Oxford University Hospitals, UK",
